Possible Honey Mustard Dressing Recipe:

Your memory of "honey...mustard...olive oil" is the perfect starting point. The key is to balance the sweet, tangy, and savory notes. Here's a simple, classic recipe you likely improvised:

Ingredients:

2 tablespoons Dijon mustard (or any good quality yellow mustard)

1 tablespoon honey

2 tablespoons olive oil

1 tablespoon white wine vinegar (or apple cider vinegar)

A pinch of salt

Freshly ground black pepper to taste

Instructions:

In a small bowl, whisk together the mustard, honey, and vinegar until they are well combined.

Slowly drizzle in the olive oil while continuously whisking. This will help the dressing emulsify, making it creamy and thick.

Add a pinch of salt and black pepper to taste. Adjust the sweetness and tanginess as needed by adding a little more honey or vinegar.

